{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773182820,"nonce":"MxG8h2jPsoyGr3ZSuMRfbc82XTE=","title":"Auth queue: no support for direct commits to protected branch (merge-only)","message":"Currently auth requests are exclusively for branch merges — there is no mechanism to submit a direct commit to the protected branch through the auth queue. This is by design (all work goes through feature branches), but worth documenting as an explicit constraint.\n\nIf a use case for direct protected-branch commits ever arises (e.g., hotfixes), the auth queue would need a new request type. For now, this is informational — direct commits are unsupported and not needed.","files":null}]}